Source: ps3-desktop
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), sudo
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ps3-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ps3-system (>= 0.367~), dbus-user-session, sudo, xserver-xorg-core, xserver-xorg-legacy,
 xinit, xauth, x11-xserver-utils, x11-utils, xinput, xserver-xorg-input-joystick,
 xserver-xorg-input-libinput, openbox, tint2, jgmenu, pcmanfm, desktop-base, greybird-gtk-theme,
 papirus-icon-theme, dunst, lxpolkit, lxterminal, network-manager-applet, pnmixer, gvfs, udev,
 systemd, procps, util-linux, python3, libxres1
Recommends: blueman, ps3-games
Description: PS3 desktop (Openbox on the RSX, game mode)
 Automatic login on tty1 (/etc/default/ps3-desktop: PS3_DESKTOP_USER) into an Openbox desktop on
 the RSX (Xorg modesetting with glamor): tint2 panel, PCManFM desktop, network, volume and
 notification helpers. Game mode keeps a game and X resident; while it runs the rest of the
 desktop gets out of the way (frozen, its memory pushed out) and comes back intact when the last
 game exits, however it exits; the game's own files are read back at its start in one pass in disk
 order, from what it used the last time. It starts by itself for any fullscreen 3D program
 (ps3-game-detect; browsers and video players excepted) and with the menu's games (ps3-game);
 PS3_GAME_MODE=off in a program's environment, or system-wide, turns it off. Gamepads move the
 pointer outside games. Shut down and Reboot menu entries, OpenArena's PS3 settings.

Package: ps3-apps
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, mousepad, gpicview, zathura, zathura-pdf-poppler, xarchiver, galculator,
 lxtask, scrot, mpv
Description: everyday desktop applications for the PS3
 Light GTK applications that suit 256 MB of RAM: a text editor (Mousepad), an image viewer
 (GPicView), a PDF viewer (zathura), an archive manager (Xarchiver), a calculator (Galculator),
 a task manager (LXTask), screenshots (scrot, on the Print key) and a media player (mpv). The
 PS3 desktop opens files with them by default. Remove this package to remove them.

Package: ps3-games
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, openarena, classicube, quakespasm, yamagi-quake2,
 armagetronad, neverball, xmoto, extremetuxracer, dsda-doom, freedoom, openttd, openttd-opengfx,
 openttd-opensfx, openttd-openmsx
Description: the PS3's game suite
 The games this distribution is tested and benchmarked with (docs/GAME-PLAN.md): each one known to
 run on the RSX, with its sound, joins this package once it does. Remove this package to remove
 them. Only free packages: the licensed game data (Quake, Quake II, ClassiCube) is in
 ps3-games-licensed.
